  "tier": "T2",
  "governed_construct": "A class declaration or class expression (ClassDeclaration / ClassExpression node). Each class is one instance.",
  "interpretation": "The rule is read as: classes must not use implementation inheritance. A class conforms when it has no `extends` heritage clause; it may implement interfaces (`implements`), hold collaborators as fields or constructor parameters, or use helper functions. A class violates when it has an `extends` clause, whatever the base: a user class, an abstract class, a framework base such as React.Component, a built-in such as Error, or a mixin-produced base (including anonymous class expressions `class extends Base`). Interface `extends` is type composition, not class inheritance, and is neither an instance nor a violation; generic constraints such as `<T extends X>` are not inheritance. Files with no class at all are NOT_APPLICABLE, even if they compose functions. Prototype manipulation (Object.create, setPrototypeOf) is out of scope. Mentions of `extends` in comments, strings or template literals are not code and do not count.",
